Intel media driver (Debian package intel-media-va-driver-non-free) and the oneVPL runtime (libmfx-gen1.2, libvpl2)
  For hardware encoding through Quick Sync. The media driver is MIT (Expat), with parts under BSD-3-Clause; Debian
  files it under non-free because its GPU kernels ship as prebuilt binaries, and it is redistributable. The oneVPL
  runtime and dispatcher are MIT.
  Source: https://github.com/intel/media-driver, https://github.com/intel/vpl-gpu-rt and https://github.com/intel/libvpl.

Every other package in the image comes from Debian 13 (the node:24-trixie-slim base and the libraries ffmpeg uses),
each under the licence in its /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. Source: Debian's source package of the installed
version (`dpkg -l` lists them), from `apt-get source <package>`, https://sources.debian.org or
